  "estimatedLength": "35 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Identify the four heart chambers and their relative locations (right atrium, right ventricle, left atrium, left ventricle).",
    "Differentiate the four major cardiac valves and describe the direction of flow they permit/prevent.",
    "Trace the path of blood through the heart and name the major entering/leaving vessels (SVC/IVC, pulmonary arteries/veins, aorta).",
    "Explain dual-loop circulation as two connected circuits (pulmonary and systemic) driven by the heart.",
    "Justify why the left ventricle has thicker myocardium based on its workload (systemic circulation).",
    "Describe how valves prevent backflow during the cardiac cycle using the visual flow sequence."
  ],
